# runtime state, not source
#
# data/memory.json is rewritten by the notebook every time memory compresses,
# so tracking it guaranteed a merge conflict on every pull — and resolving one
# by hand means picking somebody's stale general_memory, which then goes into
# the system prompt of every single response until it is overwritten.
#
# It regenerates on first run. Nothing here is worth versioning.
data/memory.json
